# Reuse and consolidate first

Before writing a helper, handler, formatter, validator, or calculation, search `src/lib/` (util, tool, service, server, model). If a function already does the job, import it. If it is the same logic with a small difference, add a parameter to that function. Do not add a near-copy.

## No local duplicates in routes

Do not declare a helper inside `+page.svelte`, `+page.ts`, `+page.server.ts`, `+layout.svelte`, `+layout.server.ts`, `+server.ts`, or a component when the same logic exists or will be needed in a second file. Move it under `$lib` and import it. Route files stay thin.

## Where new code goes

Do not create `src/lib/utils/`, `src/lib/services/`, `src/lib/api/`, or `src/lib/types/`. This repo already has those roles:

- Pure logic, parsers, formatters → `src/lib/util/`
- Shared client fetch and domain helpers → `src/lib/tool/` (setup-required helpers → `src/lib/service/`)
- DB, secrets, authz → `src/lib/server/`
- Shared JSON and UI types → `src/lib/model/type/`
- Shared UI → `src/lib/component/`

No barrel `index.ts` unless one already exists for that folder.

## One function, parameters

A second function for a slight variation (empty placeholder, page size, care setting, sales mode, IUM list vs default unit) is a duplicate. Add a parameter.

```ts
// BAD — local copy in +page.svelte
function formatDateTime(value: string | null) {
	if (!value) return '–';
	return new Date(value).toLocaleString('en-US', {
		dateStyle: 'short',
		timeStyle: 'short'
	});
}

// GOOD
import { formatMenziesTableDateTime } from '$lib/util/menzies-table-datetime.util';
formatMenziesTableDateTime(value, '–');
```
